; Load one block from tape, restart the game on an error
;
; Calls the ROM's LD-BYTES. If it reports success (carry set) the routine
; returns. If the block is bad or the load is stopped, it prints "Tape error -
; hit any key to restart program." in the input window, waits for a key and
; jumps to #R$6C27, which restores the starting state and begins a
; new game: the blocks already read have overwritten the running game.
; .
; Hardware: the ROM tape loader LD-BYTES; the keyboard port $FE.
;
; A Flag byte of the block
; F Carry set to load
; IX Address to load to
; DE Length of the block
; O:F Carry set when loaded (otherwise the routine does not return)
@label=LoadBlock
c$8498 CALL $0556    ;
 $849B RET C         ; loaded
 $849C LD A,$01      ;
 $849E LD ($B701),A  ; print in the input window
 $84A1 LD HL,$B357   ; "Tape error -     hit any key to restart program."
 $84A4 CALL $72DD    ;
@label=LoadBlock_WaitKey
*$84A7 XOR A         ; select all keyboard half-rows
@isub=IN A,(PORT_ULA)
 $84A8 IN A,($FE)    ;
@isub=AND KEY_BITS
*$84AA AND $1F       ;
@isub=CP KEY_BITS
 $84AC CP $1F        ;
 $84AE JR Z,$84A7    ; no key down yet
 $84B0 JP $6C27      ; restart
